🎬 MiniMax H3 Can Make Infinite Length Videos Now

MiniMax H3 is everywhere right now, but everyone is still stuck at one prompt, one short clip. This video breaks down the MiniMax H3 Motion Director, a node that gives you a full shot timeline inside ComfyUI. Add a shot, write its prompt, add another shot, write that one, hit run, and it generates them in order while carrying motion and audio from each shot into the next.

The important part is that every segment still generates on its own, so your GPU is never holding a 30 second video in memory. Length stops being a VRAM problem. I go through the full workflow, the model switch for first/last frame vs reference to video, the four step turbo LoRA, the attention and chunking optimizations, and then run real generations to compare character consistency between image to video and reference to video using a character sheet. The workflow is free in my Discord.

